WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.668
-Now, Michelle,
on "Downton Abbey,"

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.805
you play the extremely proper,
unshakable Lady Mary Crawley,

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.074
who speaks in
a very dignified tone.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.141
-That's right.

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:10.310
-Ah, well.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.677
I wanted to try a game with you.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:13.212
I thought it would be fun
if we took turns

00:00:13.212 --> 00:00:15.615
complaining about everyday,
annoying things,

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:18.718
but in the fanciest,
most highbrow way possible.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.220
It is time for "How Dare You?"

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.788
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:25.324
-♪ How dare you ♪

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:29.161
♪ How dare you, ah ♪

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:31.164
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.332
[ Harpsichord music playing ]

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:36.803
-Dearest Oreo Thins,

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.806
I would like to address you
for a brief moment, if I may.

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.442
Now, I will admit that at times
I certainly do appreciate

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.511
a novelty, an unconventionality,

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.580
a peculiarity of form,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.516
but this is quite simply
a bridge too far.

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:53.419
When one thinks of an Oreo,
what is brought to mind

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:56.489
is not a diminutive,
cracker-like wafer!

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.592
Any true Oreo should have
the substantial girth

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.927
of a genuine sandwich cookie!

00:01:01.927 --> 00:01:05.365
Oreo Thins, you are a travesty
and an embarrassment,

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:08.500
which is why I am sadly left
with no choice but to say,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.102
"How dare you?"

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.137
[ Slap ]

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.438
-How dare you?

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.472
[ Slap ]

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.808
-How dare you, I say!

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.877
[ Slap ]
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.513
-I would like to steal a moment
if I could, Jimmy,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:25.117
to address a most unfortunate
and unsatisfactory acquaintance.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:28.554
I am naturally speaking
of that putrid invention,

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.956
the air mattress.

00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:35.060
If I had a predilection for
sleeping inside a bouncy castle,

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.499
I would spend the night
inside a Chuck E. Cheese.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.903
You are good at neither holding
air, nor being a mattress.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:47.507
You leave me bone-weary
and with only one thing to say.

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.976
How dare you?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:53.112
-How dare you, air mattresses?

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.146
[ Slap ]

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:55.347
-How dare!

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:57.950
[ Slap ]

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.153
-Michelle, there is something

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:03.656
that I must get off my chest.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:04.957
-By all means.

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.826
-[ Clears throat ]

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:11.097
To whom it may concern,
in regards to

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.532
airline patrons who place
their heavy winter coats

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:14.934
in the overhead bin.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.805
That is a sacred space
for bags and bags alone.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.440
Perchance you accidently
put your manners in the bin,

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:24.109
as well, for it appears
you have none.

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:26.445
Place your wares under the seat
like the rest of us,

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:28.413
and good day to you, sir!

00:02:28.413 --> 00:02:29.782
-"Good day," he said.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.951
-I said, "Good day!"

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.419
[ Slap ]

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.788
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:39.091
-Jimmy, Jimmy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:41.127
-Yes?
-Jimmy, I --

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.562
Jimmy, I fear
I have another grievance.

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:44.964
-The floor is yours.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.765
-How dare you,

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:50.069
the movie "Hustlers"?
For I saw you on Friday night,

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:53.506
and now I can think nor speak
of nothing else.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:57.409
I have fallen into
a post-"Hustlers" despair.

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:59.846
J.Lo, Constance Wu,

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:03.015
Lizzo, Cardi B. all in one film,

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:05.551
and J.Lo is 50.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.654
Why does she look this way?

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.054
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:11.690
I should have brought
my smelling salts to the cinema,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.494
for I nearly passed out
numerous times.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:17.430
That many powerful women
in one film

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.432
is simply an overload
of the senses

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:22.368
that left me breathless,
gasping for air.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:26.138
And for that, again,
I say, "How dare you?"

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:27.607
[ Slap ]

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:28.875
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.344
-How dare you, "Hustlers"?!

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.379
[ Slap ]
And how da--

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.515
And how dare you, J.Lo?

00:03:36.515 --> 00:03:38.818
[ Slap ]

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.453
-How dare you look that good,
J.Lo?

00:03:41.453 --> 00:03:42.588
[ Slap ]

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:44.490
-What will we see now?

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.325
Only one film
can top "Hustlers,"

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.227
and that's "Downton Abbey,"
of course.

00:03:48.227 --> 00:03:50.796
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:51.831
[ Slap, slap ]

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.265
-Naturally.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.067
-Shall we do one more?

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:56.402
Shall we do one more together?
[ Slap ]

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:59.238
-Yes.
-I, Jimmy Fallon.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.340
-And I, Michelle Dockery.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.277
-Have a bone to pick with bees.
-Have a bone to pick with bees.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:08.481
-Sting me once,
shame on you.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.749
-Sting me twice, shame on me.

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:13.319
-Sting me three times?

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.621
-How dare you?
-How dare you?

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.423
[ Slap, slap ]

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:20.326
-How dare you,
and good day to you, sir!

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.560
-Good day.
-Good day!

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:22.628
-Good day!
-How dare you?

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.130
-How dare you?

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.297
[ Slap, slap ]

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:26.733
-My thanks to Michelle Dockery!

